      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "In patients with angina of effort all links in the system of microcirculatory hemostasis are activated and closely interconnected. Changes in one and the same index could be compensatory and pathological and it should be taken into account in attempts to interfere in the system of hemostasis. Lipid metabolic derangement in patients with angina of effort should be regarded as one of the most unfavorable factors in a course of disease. The prevention of angina attacks in such patients means the prevention of atherosclerosis progression."},
